{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1352,1478p;1820,1862p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1352\t### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\n  1353\t\n  1354\tNames live outside the manifest. A name environment maps a module name\n  1355\tto a manifest address and is linker-local state in one of two shapes:\n  1356\t\n  1357\t- a plain map `{'my.lib :segment/...}`, for tests and single-process\n  1358\t  compositions, with the composition itself as the sole asserter;\n  1359\t- assertions read from a `dao.space` source under the policy below.\n  1360\t\n  1361\t**Fail-closed assertion policy.** This policy is an entry criterion for\n  1362\tM4: no linker may resolve a name from `dao.space` assertions before it is\n  1363\timplemented and tested.\n  1364\t\n  1365\t- **Every authority event is a signed envelope.** An assertion and a\n  1366\t  retraction are two distinct envelope shapes, each a plain map whose\n  1367\t  content address (`dao.jing/segment-key`) is the event's id:\n  1368\t\n  1369\t  ```clojure\n  1370\t  ;; assertion\n  1371\t  {:yin.module/op          :assert\n  1372\t   :yin.module/name        'my.lib\n  1373\t   :yin.module/manifest    :segment/...\n  1374\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\n  1375\t   :yin.module/seq         41}          ; per-principal, strictly rising\n  1376\t\n  1377\t  ;; retraction: bound to one assertion by that assertion's id\n  1378\t  {:yin.module/op          :retract\n  1379\t   :yin.module/of          :segment/... ; segment-key of the assertion\n  1380\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\n  1381\t   :yin.module/seq         42}\n  1382\t  ```\n  1383\t\n  1384\t  The envelope is transacted as datoms `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]`\n  1385\t  and `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]`. An envelope is honored only with\n  1386\t  a proof; a bare `:asserted-by` value is a string anyone can write.\n  1387\t  An envelope whose proof is absent or fails is `:unauthenticated`\n  1388\t  with `:kind :no-proof` or `:bad-proof` and is discarded before\n  1389\t  counting. A retraction whose `:yin.module/of` names no assertion at\n  1390\t  the snapshot, or an assertion by a different principal, is discarded\n  1391\t  with `:kind :dangling-retraction`; a retraction retracts exactly the\n  1392\t  assertion it names and nothing by name alone.\n  1393\t- **Replay is prevented by the per-principal sequence.** Every envelope\n  1394\t  a principal issues carries `:yin.module/seq`, strictly increasing\n  1395\t  over that principal's lifetime; the composition declares each\n  1396\t  principal's floor in `:authority` (`0` for a new principal, the\n  1397\t  highest sequence already honored for a re-declared one). At the\n  1398\t  snapshot the linker processes one principal's proven envelopes in\n  1399\t  three passes, in this order:\n  1400\t  1. *Deduplicate by content id.* Every envelope is content; two\n  1401\t     appearances of one envelope have one `segment-key` and are one\n  1402\t     event. All but the first appearance are dropped silently, as\n  1403\t     `dao.jing` drops a re-materialization: an exact duplicate is a\n  1404\t     harmless carrier replay (a forwarder, a retry after `full`, a\n  1405\t     mirrored log) and is neither a defect nor evidence against the\n  1406\t     principal. This pass runs first so that repeating a valid envelope\n  1407\t     can never suppress it.\n  1408\t  2. *Detect equivocation.* After deduplication, two *distinct*\n  1409\t     envelopes from one principal with equal sequence are equivocation:\n  1410\t     the principal signed two different claims under one sequence\n  1411\t     number. Both are discarded with `:kind :equivocation`, and the\n  1412\t     principal's later envelopes at the snapshot are discarded too. A\n  1413\t     duplicate can no longer reach this pass, so equivocation is\n  1414\t     attributable to the signer alone.\n  1415\t  3. *Order and honor.* The remaining envelopes are ordered by sequence\n  1416\t     and each is honored only if its sequence exceeds the floor and\n  1417\t     every sequence honored before it; an envelope at or below either\n  1418\t     is a replay of an old claim under a fresh carrier and is discarded\n  1419\t     with `:kind :replay`.\n  1420\t  A monotone sequence is chosen over nonces because it makes the check\n  1421\t  stateless over the snapshot: no nonce store is needed and no window\n  1422\t  is guessed.\n  1423\t  A wall-clock timestamp is admitted as an optional\n  1424\t  `:yin.module/issued-at` in the envelope for audit, and is never used\n  1425\t  to order or to accept.\n  1426\t- Two proof kinds are admitted, and the composition's `:authority`\n  1427\t  declares, per principal, which one it expects:\n  1428\t  - *Signature.* `proof` is `{:yin.module/signature sig}`, where `sig`\n  1429\t    signs the canonical bytes (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) of the whole\n  1430\t    envelope under the principal's public key, so operation type, name,\n  1431\t    manifest, principal, and sequence are all covered and none can be\n  1432\t    altered or recombined. `:authority` holds, per principal, the key\n  1433\t    and a composition-supplied verify function; the linker calls the\n  1434\t    function and implements no cryptographic primitive itself (a host\n  1435\t    library sits behind the function, as `dao.jing` does for hashing).\n  1436\t    The signature is over content, so it survives every carrier and\n  1437\t    can be checked by any host that holds the key.\n  1438\t  - *Attested log.* The assertion stream is a one-writer log\n  1439\t    (`dao.stream.md`, *Concurrency*) whose writer the composition\n  1440\t    authenticated at attachment and bound to one principal; `:authority`\n  1441\t    names the stream's `:dao.stream/identity` beside that principal, and\n  1442\t    every envelope read from that identity, at the snapshot, counts as\n  1443\t    proven by it; `proof` is `{:yin.module/attested identity}` and the\n  1444\t    linker checks that the envelope was in fact read from that stream.\n  1445\t    The sequence rule applies unchanged, so a log that repeats an\n  1446\t    envelope repeats a replay. The proof holds only within the reach of\n  1447\t    the attachment discipline: an envelope copied off that log onto\n  1448\t    another medium carries no proof and is `:unauthenticated` there. A\n  1449\t    composition that needs envelopes to travel uses signatures.\n  1450\t  A principal declared with neither kind cannot assert anything.\n  1451\t- The linker's `:authority` names the accepted principals with their\n  1452\t  proof kind and material, and the **snapshot**: either a published\n  1453\t  index manifest address (`dao.space.index`) or a cursor position on\n  1454\t  the assertion stream. The linker reads exactly that snapshot;\n  1455\t  assertions appended afterwards do not exist for it until the\n  1456\t  composition advances the snapshot, which is an ordinary `link-state`\n  1457\t  rebuild, never an ambient re-read.\n  1458\t- At the snapshot, for one name: unauthenticated envelopes, exact\n  1459\t  duplicates beyond the first, replays, equivocations, and envelopes by\n  1460\t  undeclared principals are discarded or collapsed as the passes above\n  1461\t  say;\n  1462\t  each honored retraction removes exactly the assertion its\n  1463\t  `:yin.module/of` names; the distinct manifest addresses remaining are\n  1464\t  counted. Exactly one resolves the name. Zero is `:absent`. More than\n  1465\t  one is `:ambiguous-name` naming every remaining address and asserter,\n  1466\t  and no address is chosen by recency, sequence, order, or any other\n  1467\t  rule.\n  1468\t- Provenance is data the outcome carries: a successful resolution names\n  1469\t  the asserter, the proof kind, and the snapshot under\n  1470\t  `:yin.link/provenance` so a receiver can record which claim it acted\n  1471\t  on.\n  1472\t\n  1473\tAn entry is a claim. The manifest it names is verified, and its name is\n  1474\tverified against the entry (section 8.1). Which principals a composition\n  1475\tdeclares, and how it obtains and rotates their keys, is the composition's\n  1476\t(section 12); what the linker does with a declared principal's assertion\n  1477\tis fixed above.\n  1478\t\n  1820\t### 13.1 Revision r5 (round 4, `gpt-6-sol`)\n  1821\t\n  1822\tThe round-4 review closed round-3 item 5 and left four items partial.\n  1823\tEach, and what r5 did:\n  1824\t\n  1825\t| Item                              | Resolution                        |\n  1826\t|-----------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n  1827\t| Source order is not dominance;    | Agreed. Discharge requires an     |\n  1828\t| scanner signatures unspecified    | unconditional definition that     |\n  1829\t|                                   | dominates the occurrence; a       |\n  1830\t|                                   | definition under `:if`, a jump    |\n  1831\t|                                   | target, or a lambda body          |\n  1832\t|                                   | discharges nothing and the        |\n  1833\t|                                   | obligation is retained; scanners  |\n  1834\t|                                   | are position-bearing with a fixed |\n  1835\t|                                   | result shape (`:at`, `:in-body?`, |\n  1836\t|                                   | `:conditional?`), and a scanner   |\n  1837\t|                                   | with no positions degrades to     |\n  1838\t|                                   | retaining every obligation (4.1,  |\n  1839\t|                                   | 4.2 step 5a).                     |\n  1840\t| Scalar id in `:link-response`     | Agreed. Now `[:t0 7]` (7.2).      |\n  1841\t| Loaders reset registers; walker   | Agreed. `attach-image` per kernel |\n  1842\t| closure body is a node            | extends code space only, leaving  |\n  1843\t|                                   | pc, stack, frames, continuation,  |\n  1844\t|                                   | control, and store untouched;     |\n  1845\t|                                   | `yin.repl` becomes attach plus a  |\n  1846\t|                                   | pc set. Walker closures lift by   |\n  1847\t|                                   | locating the `:lambda` row whose  |\n  1848\t|                                   | body slot is the node, lower by   |\n  1849\t|                                   | decoding that row's body in the   |\n  1850\t|                                   | parent; an unrooted body refuses  |\n  1851\t|                                   | the lift (7.3).                   |\n  1852\t| Equal-sequence discard is a       | Agreed. Three passes: dedupe by   |\n  1853\t| denial-of-service vector          | content id first (duplicates are  |\n  1854\t|                                   | harmless and honored once), then  |\n  1855\t|                                   | equivocation over distinct        |\n  1856\t|                                   | envelopes only, then order and    |\n  1857\t|                                   | honor by sequence (8.2).          |\n  1858\t\n  1859\t### 13.2 Revision r4 (round 3, `gpt-6-sol`)\n  1860\t\n  1861\tThe round-3 review closed round-2 items 1, 3, 5, 7, and 10 and left four\n  1862\tpartial plus one example defect. Each, and what r4 did:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
