{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '932,970p;1550,1640p;1725,1776p'\"","aggregated_output":"   932\t   give each scheduler a distinct origin prefix as composition data;\n   933\t   two schedulers on one pair with one prefix is a host assembly defect.\n   934\t4. **The request is appended; `ok` moves the entry to the response\n   935\t   state.** The handler appends `:envelope` through the link request\n   936\t   writer the composition supplied in `opts`. On `ok` the entry becomes\n   937\t   `{:reason :link-response :link-id [:t0 7] :response ... :cursor ...}`.\n   938\t   On\n   939\t   `full` the entry stays in `:link-request` with its envelope retained\n   940\t   verbatim and is retried on the next poll, the `:ffi-request`\n   941\t   discipline. The two states are the two UCF pending variants this\n   942\t   flow adds (section 11, item 10): `:link-request` carries everything\n   943\t   needed to rebuild the envelope, `:link-response` carries the response\n   944\t   descriptor and the kept cell.\n   945\t5. **The linker interpreter observes the request stream** with its own\n   946\t   cursor, in its own control flow. It resolves the name through its\n   947\t   name environment at the snapshot it was composed with (section 8.2),\n   948\t   fetches the manifest by address through the `:yin.module/manifest`\n   949\t   format record so the manifest itself passes steps 2 to 4, checks the\n   950\t   manifest's declared name (section 8.1), selects the derivation and\n   951\t   identity for the requested format, verifies the derivation, and runs\n   952\t   the six steps for the image through the stepped core. A manifest with\n   953\t   no derivation for the requested format is `:unsupported-format`, and\n   954\t   the composed `:fallback` policy (section 5.5) applies, under the\n   955\t   composed `:derivation` policy, before a refusal is appended.\n   956\t6. **The response is appended** to the link response stream with the\n   957\t   request's exact `:yin.link/id`, as `:ok` with the image, manifest,\n   958\t   derivation, and obligations, or as the refusal. The linker holds\n   959\t   nothing afterwards.\n   960\t7. **`check-wait-set` polls each `:link-response` entry's kept cursor and\n   961\t   restores only on exact correlation.** On each poll the entry advances\n   962\t   past every response whose `:yin.link/id` is not its own, keeping its\n   963\t   cursor at the first unconsumed position, and acts only on a response\n   964\t   whose id equals `:link-id`. This is the per-cell round-order\n   965\t   discipline UCF section 7.5.3 already gives shared cursors, so a\n   966\t   parked `:link-response` lifts and lowers as any other wait does.\n   967\t   Handling of every other case is fixed:\n   968\t   - *duplicate*: a second response for an id whose entry has already\n   969\t     restored is skipped; ids are `[origin counter]` pairs minted once\n   970\t     and never reused, so the entry cannot exist again;\n  1550\tpredecessor namespace is renamed, not aliased.\n  1551\t\n  1552\t```mermaid\n  1553\tflowchart TD\n  1554\t  M1[\"M1 rename\\nyin.vm.debruijn-linker -> yin.vm.linker\"]\n  1555\t  M2[\"M2 four format records\\nidentity-directed match, bounded parts\"]\n  1556\t  M3[\"M3 stepped core + link runtime\\nfetch = host policy; DHT behind server\"]\n  1557\t  M4[\"M4 require lowers to the linker\\nmanifests, authority, child install\"]\n  1558\t  M5[\"M5 yin.repl wires the four streams\\nper backend\"]\n  1559\t  M1 --> M2 --> M3 --> M4 --> M5\n  1560\t```\n  1561\t\n  1562\t**M1. Rename.** Move `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc` to\n  1563\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc` with namespace `yin.vm.linker`; move the\n  1564\ttest likewise. Update the five design documents that name the old\n  1565\tnamespace (`yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md`, `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`,\n  1566\t`dao.agent.md`, `dao.agent.harness.md`, `dao.agent.mcp.server.md`) and\n  1567\tthe orchestrator log. Mark `yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md` as superseded by\n  1568\tthis document in its status line. No behavior changes. The B6 test\n  1569\tsuite passes unchanged apart from the require alias.\n  1570\t\n  1571\t**M2. Four format records.** Replace `:hash-fn` with `:identity-fn` and\n  1572\t`:identity-matches-fn`; rename `:free-names-fn` to `:obligations-fn`;\n  1573\tadd `:contract`, `:row-defect-fn`, and `:parts-fn`; add `ast-format`,\n  1574\t`semantic-format`, `semantic-free-names`, and `row-local-defect`. Make\n  1575\tstep 2 the bounded worklist. `yin.vm.content` keeps `materialize-tree!`\n  1576\tand `materialize-vector!` as the mint side (they are `publish!` for those\n  1577\tformats); `load-rows` and `fetch-vector` are retired, and their callers\n  1578\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1579\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1580\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1581\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1582\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1583\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1584\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1585\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1586\t`:blake3`.\n  1587\t\n  1588\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1589\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.remote.step` (or, for a\n  1590\tpurely local composition, over `dao.stream.rpc` on a ring-buffer pair\n  1591\tserved by `dao.jing.remote/serve-content!`'s handlers). Reimplement\n  1592\t`fetch` as the blocking driver over a link runtime; export `verify` and\n  1593\t`discharge`. Tests: the full refusal matrix through `step` over ring\n  1594\tbuffers on all three hosts; the JVM WebSocket path from B6 completion\n  1595\tcriterion 1; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\n  1596\tpart per step; a request carrying a function or a handle is\n  1597\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  1598\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  1599\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  1600\tthe server driven by the test.\n  1601\t\n  1602\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  1603\tassertion policy is implemented and its tests pass (a signed assertion\n  1604\tby a declared principal resolves; a bare `:asserted-by` with no proof is\n  1605\t`:unauthenticated`; a bad signature is `:unauthenticated`; an attested\n  1606\tlog's assertion copied onto another stream is `:unauthenticated`; an\n  1607\tundeclared principal is ignored; a signed retraction bound to an\n  1608\tassertion's id removes that assertion only, and a retraction naming no\n  1609\tassertion or signed by another principal is discarded; an exact\n  1610\tduplicate envelope is honored once and never counted as equivocation;\n  1611\ta replayed sequence and a distinct equivocating pair are discarded; two\n  1612\tproven assertions refuse `:ambiguous-name`; snapshot advance). Then:\n  1613\tthe manifest and derivation\n  1614\tformat records; `register-host-module` with profile enforcement;\n  1615\t`require-handler` minting, parking, and emitting; the two wait states\n  1616\tthrough `check-wait-set` with id correlation; the install child in the\n  1617\tscheduler with the section 7.3 phases; `link-module`; the UCF table\n  1618\tamendments. Tests, per backend: a require of an unlinked module over\n  1619\tring buffers completes and the program resumes with its exports bound;\n  1620\ta manifest declaring a different name is `:module-name-mismatch`; a\n  1621\tmanifest whose semantic, H, or R derivation leads from a different tree\n  1622\tis `:derivation-mismatch` (three swapped-image tests, and a fourth\n  1623\twhere the `:yin.ast/code` tree is not the manifest's tree); a\n  1624\tsame-named primitive of different profile at the receiver is\n  1625\t`:unresolved-free`; a shadowed export name in the requiring program's\n  1626\tstore is `:shadowed-free`; a free name the manifest never declares is\n  1627\t`:undeclared-free`; two outstanding requires on one response stream\n  1628\teach restore on their own id; a response landing before the entry would\n  1629\thave been polled is not skipped; a module requiring another links\n  1630\ttransitively while a third task keeps running; a require cycle is\n  1631\t`:require-cycle`; `(vm :stack)` and `(vm :register)` in `yin.repl` link\n  1632\tthe same manifest by H and R respectively and produce B0-equal results.\n  1633\t\n  1634\t**M5. `yin.repl` wiring.** The REPL composes the link pair per VM and\n  1635\tthe content pair per connection (`connect` already opens the RPC\n  1636\tclient). `(require 'foo)` at the prompt exercises the whole path.\n  1637\t\n  1638\tCoexistence during M4: host modules are entered by\n  1639\t`register-host-module` from the first commit of M4, so every existing\n  1640\tcomposition keeps working while linked modules are added. There is no\n  1725\t    parked entry of each kind lifts and lowers through UCF's round-trip\n  1726\t    test.\n  1727\t13. Every swapped-image and swapped-name case in M4 refuses before load.\n  1728\t14. The assertion policy of section 8.2 refuses `:ambiguous-name`,\n  1729\t    discards unproven assertions as `:unauthenticated`, and ignores\n  1730\t    undeclared principals, at a fixed snapshot.\n  1731\t15. A module that defines a name and then reads it produces no\n  1732\t    obligation for that name; a main-sequence read before the\n  1733\t    definition is `:use-before-definition`; a read inside a body\n  1734\t    defined later in the main sequence produces no obligation; a name\n  1735\t    defined only inside an `:if` branch and read afterwards retains\n  1736\t    its obligation and links only if the manifest declares it; a\n  1737\t    format whose scanner returns no positions retains every\n  1738\t    obligation; an export whose key is computed at run time is neither\n  1739\t    refused statically nor assumed, and is verified at `validated`.\n  1740\t16. Two install children and the root task, each with counter `0`,\n  1741\t    issue three requests on one link pair with three distinct ids, and\n  1742\t    each restores on its own.\n  1743\t17. On every backend, an exported closure applied in the parent after\n  1744\t    `linked` runs the same body it ran in the child; a stack and a\n  1745\t    register closure exported from a child whose image was appended at\n  1746\t    a nonzero offset in the parent resolve to the relocated pc; a\n  1747\t    walker closure lowers to a body structurally equal to the child's;\n  1748\t    on every backend, a parent parked mid-program at a nonzero pc with\n  1749\t    a non-empty stack, frames, and continuation resumes after\n  1750\t    `attach-image` at the same pc with the same stack, frames, and\n  1751\t    restore identities, and every register the loader would have reset\n  1752\t    is unchanged.\n  1753\t18. Under `:derivation :verifying`, a manifest whose record names a\n  1754\t    profile the linker does not implement is `:unverified-derivation`,\n  1755\t    never installed; under `:trusted` the same manifest installs with\n  1756\t    `:trust :composition` in the outcome.\n  1757\t19. A request naming a mismatched contract is refused with no content\n  1758\t    request appended and no validator run.\n  1759\t20. A closure re-exported from a transitive dependency lifts with that\n  1760\t    dependency's image as origin, the parent loads that image before\n  1761\t    lowering, and an origin the scheduler never verified is\n  1762\t    `:foreign-image`; a positional marker offered to a named kernel is\n  1763\t    `:binding-mismatch`.\n  1764\t21. An exact duplicate of a valid envelope, appended any number of\n  1765\t    times, is honored exactly once and never marks its principal as\n  1766\t    equivocating; a replayed envelope with an old sequence, an envelope\n  1767\t    at or below a principal's floor, two distinct envelopes with one\n  1768\t    sequence, a retraction naming no assertion, and a retraction by\n  1769\t    another principal are each discarded with the stated kind; a\n  1770\t    retraction bound to an assertion's id removes that assertion only.\n  1771\t22. One four-way manifest links through all four kernels with no\n  1772\t    `:contract-mismatch`; a manifest of another schema version is\n  1773\t    `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:schema`; a derivation without a\n  1774\t    contract entry is `:descriptor-defect` with rule\n  1775\t    `:contract-missing`.\n  1776\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
