{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1643,1685p;1777,1817p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1643\t## 10. File box\n  1644\t\n  1645\t```text\n  1646\tRenamed:  src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc\n  1647\t            -> src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc            (M1)\n  1648\t          test/yin/vm/debruijn_linker_test.cljc\n  1649\t            -> test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc           (M1)\n  1650\tNew:      test/yin/vm/linker_step_test.cljc           (M3)\n  1651\t          test/yin/vm/linker_authority_test.cljc      (M4 entry)\n  1652\t          test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc        (M4)\n  1653\tEdited:   src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc                 (M4)\n  1654\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc  (:link-request, :link-response,\n  1655\t                                        :install wait reasons; the\n  1656\t                                        install child)             (M4)\n  1657\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/content.cljc (retire load-rows,\n  1658\t                                        fetch-vector)              (M2)\n  1659\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc, semantic.cljc,\n  1660\t          debruijn/stack.cljc, debruijn/register.cljc\n  1661\t            (attach-image; offset table on the positional\n  1662\t             kernels; row index on the walker)                     (M4)\n  1663\t          src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc  (append-*-image over attach-image;\n  1664\t                                   the four streams)          (M4, M5)\n  1665\t          docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\n  1666\t            (section 7.4.1 rows, section 7.4.3 variants)           (M4)\n  1667\tDepends:  dao.jing (segment-key, segment-matches?, materialize!)\n  1668\t          dao.jing.remote, dao.jing.remote.step, dao.stream.rpc\n  1669\t          yin.vm (validate-rows, free-names, primitive-profiles)\n  1670\t          yin.vm.code (well-formed-vector?)\n  1671\t          yin.vm.ledger (derive-record, verify-derivation)\n  1672\t          yin.vm.debruijn-code, yin.vm.debruijn-register-code\n  1673\tMust not change:\n  1674\t          image-hash, register-hash, segment-key, the opcode\n  1675\t          tables, dao.stream, dao.jing, any kernel's step function\n  1676\t```\n  1677\t\n  1678\t`yin.vm.linker` exports: `fetch`, `verify`, `discharge`, `link-state`,\n  1679\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon`, `publish!`, `ast-format`,\n  1680\t`semantic-format`, `stack-format`, `register-format`, `manifest-format`,\n  1681\t`record-format`, the four free-name scanners, the four definition\n  1682\tscanners, `row-local-defect`, `index-from-datoms`, `address-attribute`,\n  1683\t`trusted-fallback`, `verifying-fallback`, `refused`, `refused?`, `ok?`,\n  1684\t`refusal-reasons`.\n  1685\t\n  1777\t## 12. Open decisions\n  1778\t\n  1779\tRecorded so a later plan does not rediscover them. None blocks M1 to M3;\n  1780\tthe first concerns material the composition supplies to a policy section\n  1781\t8.2 fixes.\n  1782\t\n  1783\t- **Key material and rotation.** Section 8.2 fixes the two proof kinds\n  1784\t  and what the linker does with a proven, unproven, or undeclared\n  1785\t  assertion. How a composition obtains a principal's public key, rotates\n  1786\t  it, and revokes it, and which signature scheme the composition-supplied\n  1787\t  verify function implements, are composition decisions. A key-rotation\n  1788\t  event is itself a candidate signed envelope under the same policy,\n  1789\t  with its own `:yin.module/op`, which a later design may take up.\n  1790\t- **Runtime capability confinement of host modules.** Section 8.3 names\n  1791\t  the host module as the trusted composition boundary and the capability\n  1792\t  discipline of `docs/agents/advanced-concepts.md` as the only run-time\n  1793\t  enforcement. Wiring tokens into effect handlers is engine and\n  1794\t  composition work outside this document.\n  1795\t- **SCC identity.** B7 hashes a mutually recursive component as one unit\n  1796\t  with canonical member ordering. Whether that unit is a manifest of\n  1797\t  manifests or a single image per format is undecided; section 7.4\n  1798\t  fixes only the response shape and the cycle refusal.\n  1799\t- **Failure policy.** Retry, deadline, and permanent absence for a\n  1800\t  `:pending` link are the composition's (D6). Whether `yin.repl` adopts\n  1801\t  the `dao.jing.remote` timing options or its own is an M5 decision.\n  1802\t- **Contract-pinned AST and semantic identities.** Strict decoupling of\n  1803\t  storage address from VM identity holds for H and R only (section 3).\n  1804\t  Pinning `:yin.ast/code` and `:yin.semantic/code` identities to a\n  1805\t  contract hash, with explicit identity-to-address indexes, is an\n  1806\t  amendment to UCF section 7.3.2 and `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` section\n  1807\t  4.1. The linker is prepared for it: `:identity-matches-fn` and\n  1808\t  `:indexes` are the only slots that would change.\n  1809\t- **A stepped DHT client.** The DHT is served behind the content\n  1810\t  boundary (section 6.1). A portable, non-blocking DHT client that could\n  1811\t  sit on the linker's side is a `dao.jing.dht` design.\n  1812\t- **Unrecognized outcomes.** `dao.stream.md` OD-1 proposes that a\n  1813\t  consumer treat an unrecognized outcome as refused and not retryable.\n  1814\t  The stepped core follows that rule once OD-1 is accepted; until then\n  1815\t  it classifies unknown content-server answers as `transport-error`, as\n  1816\t  `dao.stream.observe/step` does.\n  1817\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
