no receiver can bind it\n   463\t     identically. The definition set is **advisory for exports**: an\n   464\t     export under `:yin.module/exports` that the static scan finds is\n   465\t     known to be bound if the body halts, and one it does not find\n   466\t     (a key computed at run time) is neither refused nor assumed. Every\n   467\t     export is verified at run time in the `validated` phase of section\n   468\t     7.3, which is the only export check; revision r3's early static\n   469\t     `:export-missing` is withdrawn. An image requested by bare identity\n   470\t     with no manifest has no declarations; it verifies only if every\n   471\t     free occurrence is discharged by its own definitions, which is B6's\n   472\t     closed-image case and remains supported.\n   473\t   - *5b, at the receiver: discharge.* Obligations travel with the\n   474\t     verified image in the response. The receiver checks each against\n   475\t     its live state as the first act of installation, before any load:\n   476\t     a `:primitive` obligation is discharged only by a primitive of\n   477\t     equal profile address; a `:module` obligation only by a linked\n   478\t     module of equal manifest address; a name bound in the receiver's\n  1011\t- **The child is a task, not a call.** The scheduler holds\n  1012\t  `:installs {name {:phase p :vm child :waiters [task-ids] :parent\n  1013\t  link-id}}`. The child is a VM of the same backend with a fresh,\n  1014\t  isolated store containing nothing of any other task's state (UCF\n  1015\t  section 7.6.2 applied to loading), its own wait-set, and the parent's\n  1016\t  registry value as its module view. The scheduler steps it in its\n  1017\t  ordinary round beside every other task; nothing about it runs inside\n  1018\t  wait restoration.\n  1019\t- **The requiring task waits on the install, not on the linker.** Once\n  1020\t  the child starts, the parent's entry becomes\n  1021\t  `{:reason :install :name 'foo}`, and any other task that requires\n  1022\t  `'foo` meanwhile joins `:waiters`. No task is restored until the\n  1023\t  install reaches `linked` or `refused`.\n  1024\t- **`running` may park.** A module body that reads a stream, calls FFI,\n  1025\t  or requires another module parks the child exactly as any task parks;\n  1055\t  2. *The origin set is checked.* The lifted slice's\n  1056\t     `:yin.k/requires :yin.k/segments` enumerates every origin image it\n  1057\t     names, transitively through captured values. Each must be an image\n  1058\t     this scheduler verified: the module's own, or one delivered for an\n  1059\t     install in this scheduler's history (held under `:installs` or the\n  1060\t     registry by identity). An origin identity the scheduler never\n  1061\t     verified is `:foreign-image`, and the install is refused; a\n  1062\t     verified image is never re-fetched for this step.\n  1063\t  3. *The parent attaches every origin image it does not yet hold*,\n  1064\t     non-destructively. The ordinary loaders (`vm-load-rows`,\n  1065\t     `load-vector`, `load-image`) are entry points for a fresh run:\n  1066\t     they set the program counter, control, or root, and reset the\n  1067\t     operand stack and frames. The parent at `linked` is a parked task\n  1068\t     whose registers must survive, so each kernel exposes a second\n  1069\t     operation, **`attach-image`**, that extends the kernel's code\n  1070\t     space and touches nothing else. Its contract, per kernel:\n  1071\t     - *semantic*: the verified vector is added under a fresh local id\n  1072\t       and the address is written to the alias column; `:control`,\n  1073\t       `:env`, `:stack`, `:k`, every `:return` frame's segment and pc,\n  1074\t       and the store are unchanged, because existing local ids are\n  1075\t       never renumbered (UCF section 7.3.4, \"local-id immutability\n  1076\t       stands\");\n  1077\t     - *stack* and *register*: the image is relocated by the current\n  1078\t       held length and appended to `:segment` (and, for the register\n  1079\t       VM, `:bodies` shifted likewise), and one `[identity offset\n  1080\t       length]` row is appended to the **offset table**, a kernel-state\n  1081\t       vector the lift of act 1 also reads; `:pc`, `:stack`, `:frames`,\n  1082\t       `:continuation` (every `:return-pc` and `:frames` in it), and\n  1083\t       `:registers` are unchanged, because appending never moves an\n  1084\t       instruction already held; `:hash` becomes the identity of the\n  1085\t       new concatenation, as `yin.repl`'s `append-*-image` computes it;\n  1086\t     - *walker*: the verified tree's rows are added to the kernel's\n  1087\t       row set (`:code-segment` expansion) keyed by their ids; the\n  1088\t       current node, environment, and continuation are unchanged.\n  1089\t     `yin.repl`'s `append-stack-image` and `append-register-image`\n  1090\t     already do the relocation and append but then set `:pc` to the\n  1091\t     new offset to start the next input; `attach-image` is that\n  1092\t     function without the final `:pc` assignment, and `yin.repl` is\n  1093\t     rewritten to call `attach-image` and then set `:pc` itself. A\n  1094\t     parked task attached to in this way resumes at the same pc, with\n  1095\t     the same stack and frames, and every restore identity it holds\n  1096\t     (`:return-pc`, `:stack-base`, semantic `:segment` ids, cursor\n  1097\t     cells) still names what it named. An image already present is not\n  1098\t     attached twice; the alias column or the offset table says so.\n  1099\t  4. *The parent lowers the encoding* against its own coordinate space\n  1100\t     by the mapping below. The lowered slice is what the registry value\n  1101\t     gains as `:bindings`.\n  1102\t  The registry value then gains `{'foo {:manifest m :address a\n  1103\t  :derivation d :bindings lowered}}`, `resolve-var`'s module step reads\n  1104\t  `:bindings`, and every waiter is restored with `'foo` as its value.\n  1105\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
