{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'store slice|store-slice|yin.k/store|§7.6.2' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | head -n 55; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '784,830p'\"","aggregated_output":"12:3. **Dependency Closure & Context:** A parked fragment is not a complete configuration. The format must carry its complete scheduler context — required primitives *with profiles*, loaded modules, referenced parked records, the fresh-name counter, and the reachable store slice — discovered by a conservative fixed point that includes explicit store operands, and must restore into an **isolated execution store** so the receiver's own state cannot change resolution.\n100: :yin.k/store       {…}                        ; §7.6.2  the store slice restored as an isolated store\n108:`:yin.k/cells`, `:yin.k/store`, `:yin.k/scheduler`), *what world*\n546:slice of §7.6.2. The outcome is either the portable form or a refusal naming\n762:§7.6.3, the store slice, and the pending wait. Its unit of analysis is a work\n788:  discharged by a matching key in the reachable store slice, or retained as\n812:### 7.6.2 The store slice, restored as an isolated store\n822::yin.k/store {counter 41\n1187:   refusal; compute `:yin.k/requires` and `:yin.k/store` by the fixed point\n1219:7. **Restore into an isolated store** (§7.6.2): the slice, the remapped\n   784\t  (a parked id, §7.6.3). Discovering a new work item continues the fixed point\n   785\t  with that address and context even when the address was already walked for\n   786\t  another context.\n   787\t- **Names:** only a free `:var` name is an obligation. An obligation is\n   788\t  discharged by a matching key in the reachable store slice, or retained as\n   789\t  a required primitive or module export and checked by profile (§7.5.2). An\n   790\t  environment never discharges a name: captured environments contribute\n   791\t  values to their work item's reachability analysis, while lexical binding\n   792\t  determines whether a `:var` is free before it becomes an obligation. If no\n   793\t  store key or profiled primitive/module requirement can discharge an\n   794\t  obligation, discovery is `:incomplete`; after lowering, an unavailable\n   795\t  retained requirement is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` (§7.6.5).\n   796\t- **Modules:** a module's manifest declares its exported primitive profiles\n   797\t  and its **store footprint** (store keys and effect kinds its handlers may\n   798\t  touch). Until manifests carry footprints, any required module whose\n   799\t  footprint is undeclared sets `:yin.k/discovery :incomplete` — the honest\n   800\t  statement that closure could not be computed, never a silent\n   801\t  under-approximation. A module effect handler may read store keys the\n   802\t  static walk cannot see; a composition may supply extra slice keys\n   803\t  explicitly, and the value records that it did.\n   804\t\n   805\tBecause the computation is over data, the same query answers \"what does this\n   806\tprogram need?\" for a segment that has never run. And because discovery can\n   807\t*fail to terminate successfully* — a missing segment cannot be walked, an\n   808\tundeclared footprint cannot be closed — the result distinguishes\n   809\t`:complete` from `:incomplete` from `:blocked` (§7.6.5); a fixed point that\n   810\tcould not finish is reported as such, not passed off as a satisfied closure.\n   811\t\n   812\t### 7.6.2 The store slice, restored as an isolated store\n   813\t\n   814\tThe store S holds `def` results, stream handles, cursor entries, and the FFI\n   815\tpair (§4.1). None of it is global in the UCF sense; it is the emitter's. A\n   816\tcontinuation carries the **reachable slice**: every store key the fixed\n   817\tpoint of §7.6.1 can name — every free `:var` obligation for which the\n   818\temitter's store has a matching key, every `:store-get`/`:store-put` operand,\n   819\tevery stream/cursor cell — with values encoded by §7.5:\n   820\t\n   821\t```clojure\n   822\t:yin.k/store {counter 41\n   823\t              'log {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream …}}\n   824\t```\n   825\t\n   826\tThe FFI pair is never in the slice — a program that names the pair's store\n   827\tkeys directly holds handles, and the lift refuses it (§7.5.4). A resumer has\n   828\tits own pair; outstanding calls route per §7.4.3.\n   829\t\n   830\t**There is no merge.** The first draft said, in two places, both that the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-24 12:39:54 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-24 19:39:54 ICT\n\nVerdict: REJECTED\n\n1. **PARTIAL — Dominance and scanners.** Conditional definitions now retain obligations. But a read inside a lambda is still discharged by a later top-level definition even if the lambda runs first. The text says that read must error; the actual resolver may instead find a primitive or module binding whose profile was never checked. The format-record examples also still return name sets rather than the required position-bearing records. Retain the obligation unless all possible applications are proven to follow the definition, and update the record examples and scanner API. [linker.md:257](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:257), [linker.md:439](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:439), [engine.cljc:54](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:54)\n\n2. **CLOSED — Wait-entry ID.** The remaining example now uses `[:t0 7]`. [linker.md:934](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:934)\n\n3. **PARTIAL — Attachment and closure relocation.** `attach-image` avoids resetting registers, but appending changes positional `:hash`. Existing parked entries contain the old hash, and both restore functions refuse a mismatch; they also restore the entry’s old `:segment`, potentially discarding the attachment. Define hash-safe restore/rebasing before claiming a parked parent can resume. Separately, the spec lowers bindings into *one parent’s* coordinates and publishes them for every waiter, whose VMs may have different offsets or local IDs. Keep bindings portable and attach/lower per receiving task, or define a genuinely shared code space. [linker.md:1077](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1077), [linker.md:1099](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1099), [stack.cljc:230](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:230), [register.cljc:224](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:224)\n\n4. **CLOSED — Duplicate authority events.** Exact content IDs are deduplicated before distinct equal-sequence envelopes are treated as equivocation. [linker.md:1393](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1393)\n\n**Additional P1 — Module-local store is lost on export.** A child runs with an isolated store, but `linked` transfers only exported values. For `(def x 1)` followed by an exported closure reading `x`, that closure’s free read uses the *parent’s* store after relocation; `x` is not captured in its closure environment. It can fail or bind to a different value. Specify a portable, isolated module-store context for exported closures, including later writes, rather than merging child keys into the parent store. [linker.md:1011](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1011), [linker.md:1099](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1099), [engine.cljc:54](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:54), [UCF.md:812](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:812)\n\nThe 2,035-line file is pure ASCII with no lines over 80 columns. **Consensus has not been reached; r5 is not ready to commit.**"}}
